add('lesson:'+slug,'Container for authorized evidence preservation, contextual metadata/custody and independently testable recovery copies.',[
 'Profile replaces the authored title/summary; the right-order header is interpreted with explicit feasibility, safety, legal authority and approved-procedure qualifications in the sections.',
 'Observed4.8/4.9/3.4 tags are broad candidate metadata, not exact child scope. The container and nine subunits are related catalogue records, not ten independent assessments or a complete forensic/recovery programme.',
 'Related lesson/deck selection does not repair held procedure, log integrity, SSH or SQL injection sources, grant canonical links or prove post-miss recovery.'
]);
add('keywords:'+slug,'Brief definitions distinguish custody records, preservation instruction and time-based acceptable data-loss target.',[
 'Custody vocabulary is introductory rather than a complete collection/safeguarding/analysis record; it does not prove integrity, attribution or admissibility.',
 'Legal hold is a preservation instruction, with authority/trigger/scope/release dependent on jurisdiction and facts. No universal duty, actual litigation or legal advice.',
 'RPO concerns tolerated data loss measured in time, distinct from restoration duration/RTO or an achieved backup interval. No tested target, retention design or recovery guarantee.'
]);
add('check:'+slug,'Reveal-only ransomware scenario rejects assured recovery from snapshots sharing production credentials/storage.',[
 'Shared accounts and failure domain can compromise snapshots; protected independently recoverable retained copies and restore tests are recommended under the supplied premise, not proof every snapshot is unusable.',
 'A product named backup is not automatically independent or clean. The model answer gives no actual recovered system, RTO/RPO result or tested procedures.',
 'This check reveals an authored response and accepts no learner answer; no grading key, automated correctness, wrong-answer feedback or independent assessment family exists.'
]);
add('section:'+slug+':0','Prioritize fragile evidence under an authorized, feasible and safety-aware response procedure.',[
 'RAM can contain relevant artifacts but none is guaranteed present. Acquisition changes state, tools/context matter, and registers/cache can be more volatile; no universal RAM-first or photographs-first sequence.',
 'Collection, containment and operational safety may require tradeoffs. Source explicitly limits capture order to when feasible and approved procedure; no blanket keep-running or power-off rule.',
 'Legal authority and privacy depend on actual context. No host, memory image, credentials, device scene or evidence acquisition is collected here.'
]);
add('section:'+slug+':1','Use metadata as mutable contextual evidence and document evidence handling beyond technical hashes.',[
 'Timestamps/EXIF/authorship/ownership fields can be changed or misleading; a correlated record is not automatic human attribution, chronological truth or a complete timeline.',
 'Hashes support checking covered retained bytes against trusted references; they alone do not prove no omitted/deleted log events or legal admissibility. This does not repair the held Log Integrity source.',
 'Custody records include collection, analysis, transfer/storage context and controlled handling. No actual record, verified chain, trusted baseline or legal proceeding is inspected.'
]);
add('section:'+slug+':2','Four source-purpose comparisons distinguish journals, snapshots, replicas and protected recoverable retained copies.',[
 'For resilient recovery in this lesson, independent recoverable backup is the design goal, not a claim that all products called backup are automatically independent. Snapshots may form part of a backup design if protection/failure boundaries are established.',
 'Journals support recorded changes rather than a complete retained independent copy; replicas can propagate logical corruption, and snapshots can share credentials/storage. Actual features/retention and failure domains vary.',
 'Restore-tested, protected, maintained copies still require clean data, dependencies and target verification. No recovery, availability guarantee, immutable-retention enforcement, RTO/RPO attainment or four independent skills.'
]);
add('traps:'+slug,'Three cautions separate volatile-state risks, snapshot independence and contextual metadata attribution.',[
 'Shutdown can destroy evidence while continued operation can alter it; the authorized procedure determines the response. Neither a snapshot nor a metadata label supplies a complete trustworthy record.',
 'The source rarely-proves-attribution caution is not a claim that metadata is useless. Corroboration, controls and context matter; no actual malicious actor or forensic outcome is established.'
]);
